# Environment for the Vercel project.
#
# Copy the values into Vercel: Project, Settings, Environment Variables.
# There is no .env file to place on disk for this site, because everything here
# is static except a few serverless functions, and Vercel injects these into them.
#
# **Every one is optional.** The first two are the TURN relay's. Without them
# the site works, and the remote control
# pairs wherever the two devices can reach each other directly: the same wifi,
# or two networks that happen to allow it. What they add is the relay that
# makes pairing work from a phone on mobile data to a laptop on ethernet,
# which otherwise fails because a carrier usually puts a phone behind a
# symmetric NAT that STUN cannot get through.
#
# api/turn-credentials.js answers with an empty server list when they are
# missing, and the app carries on with STUN alone.
#
# The coturn side lives in turn-server/ at the repository root.

# The same string as static-auth-secret in turn-server/turnserver.conf.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Treat it as a password. Anybody holding it can mint credentials and relay
# traffic through your VPS at your expense, so it stays here and in coturn and
# nowhere else. It is never sent to a browser: the function signs short-lived
# credentials with it, and those expire within the hour.
TURN_SECRET=

# The hostname clients connect to, which is the realm in turnserver.conf.
# A name rather than a bare IP, so the turns: endpoint on 5349 can present a
# certificate for it.
TURN_HOST=turn.cue.uwuapps.org

# Optional. Defaults to TURN_HOST, and only needs setting if coturn's realm
# differs from the hostname clients dial.
# TURN_REALM=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Android app. All optional; android/FIREBASE-SETUP.md has the steps.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The UwU Apps Firebase project's service account key, the whole JSON file
# (raw or base64). api/push/release.js sends the "new version" notification
# with it. A password: it stays in Vercel and nowhere else.
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=

# The secret typed into the GitHub webhook that calls /api/push/release.
# Without it the webhook answers 503 and nothing is sent.
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# A fine-grained GitHub token with read-only access to public repositories.
# Lifts GitHub's 60-requests-an-hour limit on /api/app-release, which is cached
# for ten minutes anyway.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
